  "transcript": {
    "answer": "The event-router service was deleted as part of the ADR-044 amendment dated 2026-10-02, which folded it into lore-api. GitHub webhooks now go to lore-api's `POST /api/webhook/github`. That route verifies the HMAC signature (`X-Hub-Signature-256`, secret `LORE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) and writes `github.*` events to `pipeline.events` on lore-api's own pool. The public `/api/events` URL is unchanged. The ingresses rewrite both public webhook hostnames onto the lore-api route, so no repo hooks had to be repointed. The stations service drains and claims its own event deliveries.",
    "answered_as_json": true,
